{
  "_comment": [
    "The eventd service definition.",
    "",
    "eventd requires authd before opening its KACS-backed query surface. The",
    "registry provider is already ready before peinit enters phase 2 and is not",
    "a phase-2 service dependency; KMES and KACS are kernel facilities. The",
    "authd edge also stops eventd first, preserving shutdown events.",
    "",
    "Readiness is Notify: READY=1 means all stores and sockets are open and the",
    "synthetic.startup record is durably committed. RuntimeDirectories creates",
    "/run/eventd before launch. The package separately supplies empty protected",
    "/var/state/eventd/{events,logs,metrics} directories.",
    "",
    "ErrorControl is Critical because continuing a requested boot without the",
    "system event sink silently destroys its audit history. RestartPolicy retries",
    "ordinary crashes before peinit applies the Critical failure policy.",
    "",
    "This definition is inert until an image names eventd-service.reg in its",
    "[registry] autoapply list. The image must also apply eventd-config.reg."
  ],
  "keys": [
    { "path": "Machine\\System" },
    { "path": "Machine\\System\\Services" },
    {
      "path": "Machine\\System\\Services\\eventd",
      "values": [
        { "name": "ImagePath",          "type": "sz",    "data": "/sbin/eventd" },
        { "name": "Triggers",           "type": "multi", "data": ["boot"] },
        { "name": "RuntimeDirectories", "type": "multi", "data": ["eventd"] },
        { "name": "Requires",           "type": "multi", "data": ["authd"] },
        { "name": "Identity",           "type": "sz",    "data": "SYSTEM" },
        { "name": "Readiness",          "type": "dword", "data": 0 },
        { "name": "RestartPolicy",      "type": "dword", "data": 1 },
        { "name": "ErrorControl",       "type": "dword", "data": 1 },
        { "name": "DisplayName",        "type": "sz",    "data": "Event and observability store" },
        { "name": "Description",        "type": "sz",    "data": "Persists KMES events, service logs and metrics and serves authorized queries" }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
